+
+    Gateway signer identities (mxid / session keys) cannot be bound to the outcome contract's
+    ownerPersonId/verificationOwnerId — the people registry has no person↔mxid bridge in
+    batch 1 — so NO consent, single or two distinct signers, releases a ``dual_sign_required``
+    entry here; fail closed with an operator pointer. Batch 2 builds the bridge and reopens
+    gateway release. Deny and unrecognized answers never hold: one refusal settles the
+    request, and an unrecognized answer is refused fail-closed by the waiting side. Entries
+    without the mark are untouched. Caller holds ``_lock``."""
+    if not isinstance(entry.data, dict) or not entry.data.get("dual_sign_required"):
+        return False
